  <p>At <a href="https://augmodo.com">Augmodo</a> I sit between the cameras and the customers. Humans label our video and check our predictions; I build the tools they do it in and the pipelines that turn their judgment into data the modeling teams can train on. Teaching cameras to notice when a shelf is empty is harder than it sounds. Before that I worked on ads at Yelp: autobidding, auction dynamics, recommender systems. Before that I was a physicist, mostly <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-69816-z">X-ray imaging</a>.</p>
  <p>Born and raised in Houston. Living in London. Spending more and more time in Singapore. I've studied Chinese on and off for a decade, long enough to translate a physicist's memoir. I used to compete in Wushu, coached a few hundred people to do it better than I did, and have been the back half of a lion. I'm newly into poker and may post hand analyses here once I've lost enough money to have opinions. I also cycle, in the sense that I own a bike and occasionally fall off it.</p>
  <p>I write about ML in small companies and about leading engineers. <a href="/writing">Read this first.</a></p>

